{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779313411,"nonce":"OaZnVRHhhf9DBAE3QlNYUC8Gtac=","title":"Studio: split Model and Task top projections","message":"Split the current top-level Graph projection into separate Model and Task projections.\n\nContext:\n- This follows the task-as-scenario-boundary direction captured in bda4721 and the Studio coordination issue 93f79f2.\n- The current Graph projection mixes model graph editing, the component palette, task data, and task-to-model binding UI in one surface.\n- The intended split is a UI/projection split over the same canonical Studio scenario, not a schema split and not a reintroduction of task nodes into GraphSpec.\n\nDecisions:\n- Model projection owns model architecture editing: component palette, model graph structure, model node properties, and schema/port compatibility.\n- Task projection owns task definition and task-to-model binding authoring.\n- Task bindings remain explicit scenario binding records, not ordinary model graph component edges.\n- In Model projection, task bindings should be rendered only as read-only green source hints on the bound model input ports.\n- In Task projection, the task data pseudo-node can still be wired into model ports as the editing surface.\n- Existing saved top-pane state value graph should migrate to model.\n\nInitial implementation scope:\n- Add top projections: model, task, workspace, objectives.\n- Rename the current Graph tab to Model.\n- Move the TaskScenarioPanel out of Model and into Task.\n- Keep the canvas visible in Model and Task.\n- Preserve task-binding visualization/editing in Task.\n- Add a simple Model-view bound-port hint if feasible without larger canvas refactoring.\n- Do not implement delayed-reach task-data decomposition, dynamic mux ports, or objective inference in this issue.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Switching Model / Task / Workspace / Objectives does not grey-screen or break hook order.\n- Model view has the component sidebar and no full task sidebar.\n- Task view has the task panel and no component sidebar clutter.\n- Existing task-data binding still validates as satisfying bound model input connectivity.\n- Bound task input ports are not editable as task wires from Model view.\n- Build and focused frontend tests pass.","files":null}]}